eole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"French, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"Exh1uNhTSDR1hGivZBIylA","review_id":"n3vV9iZUc4XCj9DcDdNVKQ","date":"2016-08-29T19:48:41","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9455394148826599,"text_excerpt":"AH-MAZING! Had a romantic dinner date here thanks to Coolinary month (side note--how freakin awesome is Coolinary, definitely learned about it a little too late but can't wait to check out next year's participating restaurants--check it out for yourself!) To begin, it is a large restaurant subdivided into 4 sections. The bar area dining and the first segment of the dining hall is the most quiet. The third part of the hall is set up with large buffet tables down the center, smaller booths on the side, and the last part has round tables and two person tables. The third and fourth sections are loud! Not necessarily a bad thing but this isn't your dimly lit, keep your conversations at a whisp..."},{"business_id":"Exh1uNhTSDR1hGivZBIylA","review_id":"dG7JEZS4Tc3626Qd1r7GMQ","date":"2016-12-22T16:00:41","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9444699287414551,"text_excerpt":"Ate here for Reveillon in 2016 and it was a fantastic meal. The Reveillon menu had three soup options, ten salad/app options, nine entree options, and six dessert options. We were a party of 6 and everyone pretty much ordered something different. Let me tell you, everything that came to our table looked delicious. Not one complaint from the group. My meal was outstanding start to finish. If I had to be honest I would say there was just too much food...and all of it was too good. I woke up the next morning and still felt stuffed. But it was a special meal and I don't eat like that much anymore. Service and ambiance matched the food in every way. Can't recommend The Pelican Club enough. Go ..."},{"business_id":"Exh1uNhTSDR1hGivZBIylA","review_id":"LV1-PQ1dNQJDpPNvz5TByQ","date":"2010-09-17T00:09:45","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9443098306655884,"text_excerpt":"Local friends took us out to dinner at the Pelican Club and it was the best meal we had while visiting New Orleans. We all ordered off the Summer \"Coolinary\" menu, which offers a 3-course prix fixe menu for the low price of $35. This is a steal, as their normal 4-course prix fixe varies in price from $43 - $52. For my first course, I selected the zesty chicken, shrimp, and andouille sausage gumbo. This packed a tremendous amount of flavor and the right dose of heat. I did find a small chicken bone floating in it; the waitress noticed this when collecting our plates, apologized, and gave us complimentary hot beverages at the meal's end. I tried something a little different for my entree: t..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"Exh1uNhTSDR1hGivZBIylA","photo_id":"QTAZCBq14cs9sFlGFzrM9A","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/QTAZCBq14cs9sFlGFzrM9A.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8692628741264343},{"business_id":"Exh1